            'abstract' => 'Smart Retail Recognition System is a advanced-level project that identifies shelved products from a camera view for tasks such as automated checkout or restocking checks. The project addresses a practical need: manually scanning or checking shelved products is slow in a retail or inventory-management context. It is implemented by training or reusing an image classifier/detector on labeled product images and running it on a shelf or checkout camera feed to identify items present. The expected outcome is a working, demonstrable system that clearly shows the target AI or robotics capability in action, suitable for evaluation against the program\'s standard assessment criteria.',
