            'abstract' => 'Walking Demonstration is a beginner-level project that programs NAO to walk, turn, and stop through a short scripted routine. The project addresses a practical need: as with any humanoid platform, reliable basic locomotion is the first milestone before any reactive behavior can be layered on top. It is implemented by using NAOqi\'s motion API or Choregraphe boxes to sequence walk, turn, and stop, tested on a flat, dry, clear floor. The expected outcome is a working, demonstrable system that clearly shows the target AI or robotics capability in action, suitable for evaluation against the program\'s standard assessment criteria.',
            'introduction_background' => 'NAO-based training projects follow the same perceive-decide-act pattern as other humanoid platforms, but NAO\'s stronger built-in dialogue and Choregraphe tooling make conversational and social-interaction scenarios a more natural fit than purely locomotion-heavy ones. In the specific context of this project, the trainee will work on a system that programs NAO to walk, turn, and stop through a short scripted routine. This places the project squarely within the NAO robotics track of the training program, using Motion Programming as its primary technical foundation.',
